# Frontend

## Stack

- React 19 + Next.js App Router
- Tailwind 4 + shadcn (`@base-ui/react`)
- Icons: **Lucide** (keep — do not swap icon libraries)
- Motion: Framer Motion (already in repo)

## Design tokens (do not invent new palettes)

Per `docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md` §12:

- Brand sky: `#4ba3e8` (`--color-brand`)
- Accent pink: `#efa3bc` (`--color-accent-pink`)
- Page background: `#f7fafd`
- Cute, playful, gamified classroom — not corporate admin or Awwwards luxury

## Reuse before creating

- `src/components/classroom/*` — shared primitives
- `components/ui/*` — shadcn components
- Existing page patterns under `src/app/`

## State

- Local `useState` → lift to common ancestor → `AppDataContext` for classroom data
- Derive values during render; avoid `useEffect` to sync derived state

## Layout

- New pages render inside existing `src/app/layout.tsx` shell
- Do not create a second Sidebar or AppLayout

## Security

- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with student names or user-provided text
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations

## Touch targets

- Classroom actions (+1, spin, pick student): large enough for fast in-class use (44px minimum where practical)

## Dialogs

CRUD/scoring overlays: `useModalFocusTrap` + `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal` + labelled heading (`gift-redeem-dialog.tsx`). Stacked modals: `modalTrapStack` (top trap only). Full-screen overlays that must cover the shell: `createPortal(..., document.body)` (e.g. recognition celebration). Leave Lucky Wheel (and sibling game modals: Duck Race, Points Wheel) without a keyboard trap unless requested.
